      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-03-23_WidnesExaminer_art0008" n="art0008">
        <head>ASK EXIM GR McDOUGALL'S Paterit SELF-RAISING FLOUR</head>
        <p>ASK EXIM GR McDOUGALL'S Paterit SELF-RAISING FLOUR</p>
        <p>ENCOURAGEMENT FROM EDUCATION COMMITTEE. ST HELENS.</p>
        <p>THE ACCOMMODATION DIFFICULTY AT THE SECONDARY SCI-100L.</p>
        <p>For those Who are sick it is like a peep into the . garden of hope to receive news which gives them assur- , ance of permanent recovery. Many of us will read with I delight this encouraging news from St. Helens. " I have no objection to the facts of my cure by I Scheme to Use the Gymnasium Doan's backache kidney pills being published," says i Mrs. E. Astles, 14, Crook-street, St. Helens, "because i ----- they have done me so much good, and I think it is only 1 The Warrington Education Committee concluded right tint I should let others know how reliable the another year's work with its meeting at the Town Hall medicine is. "For three years Iqas a great sufferer from weak 'on Monday evening. Alderman Bennett presided, and there were also present :—Miss Williams, the Mayor, kidneys. I had dull, gnawing pains in the small of my I back. I could scarcely get up and down stairs, and to; Alderman Evans, Councillors Fulton Smith, Dickenson, Sankey, Ellison, Steel, Evans, Wilkinson, Pemberton raise myself after sitting was a difficult matter. Some- i times my back would crick and seemed as if it was I and Lord, Revs. Canon- ley Stevenson, J. Davies, N. Wilson and John Yo Messrs. C. E. Parker, C. giving out. I often had to take hold of something for i H. Unsworth support or I should have fallen; bending with me was i ,G. Walker, pson, A. J. Jolley., H, Roberts, C. S. Burgess, R. T. Fairclough, G. H. bang- quite out of the question. I had medicine from the I doctor, and had my back rubbed with oils,but I received (director). don, E. Plinston, T. P. Bradshaw and J. Moore Murray I no benefit. "When I began with Doan's backache kidney pills and found they were doing me good, I kept on with them. Now that I have used four boxes of the pills I am cured. Doan's pills are excellent, and I cannot praise them too highly. (Signed) Emily Astles." Among the chief symptoms of Kidney Disease are Urinary Troubles, Backache, Pains in the Loins, Dizziness, Ringing in the Ears, Tiredness and Broken Sleep. Among the most serious results of Kidney Disease are Dropsy, Gravel, Stone, Bladder Diseases, Rheu- matism, Lumbago and Sciatica. The cure for all these symptoms and diseases is to go to the root of these troubles and to cure your kidneys by taking Doan's Backache Kidney Pills. Doan's Backache Kidney Pills are two shillings and ninepence per box (six boxes for thirteen shillings and ninepence). Of all chemists and stores, or post free, direct from Foster-McClellan Co., 8, Wells-street, Oxford-street, London, W. Be sure you get exactly the same kind of pills that Mrs. Astles had.</p>
        <p>THE LATE DR. GORNALL.</p>
        <p>The DIRECTOR read a letter from Mrs. Gornall expressing her earnest thanks for the expression of regret and kind sympathy in her great loss, and also for their kind remembrance of her dear husband and expressed appreciation of his life and work.</p>
