        <p>Warrington Works Bowling Association. The sth annual meeting in connection with the above association was held last Friday evening at the Bowling Green, Bank Quay, Mr. Willett presiding over a very fair attendance from the various works. After a very successful season the Secretary pre- sented the balance sheet which showed the receipts as £6l us. 10d., expenditure £6O 18s. id., leaving a balance to be carried forward to the coming season of 13s. 9d. Mr. W. H. Smalley resigned his position as secretary and a very hearty vote of thanks was accorded him for his past services. Mr. E. Scott, of 17,Legh-street, was unanimously elected secretary and Mr. 0-. Holbrook was re-elected bon. treasurer with a committee of 11 members selected from the works. The voting for the committee resulted in the following gentlemen being elected :—T. Horrobin (London and North-Western Railway), F. Dean (White Cross), J. Willett (Crosfields), G. Ball (Pearson and Knowles), W. Simister (Longford Wire Co.), T. O'Brien (Castle Rubber Co.), W. Patrick (N. Greening and Sons), W. Randles (Fletcher Russell and (Jo.) T. Barnes (Rvlands Bros. Ltd.). J. Hutchinson (Robinsons). The Chairman remarked that last season had been a record, 133 teams taking part in the competition,and he hoped Ithat the corning season would be as great a success as the last. The new committee have matters well Linder consideration and expect within a very few days to be able to notify the works when the 1907 com- petition will commence. •</p>
        <p>W. r_i. W . CLOOGKINSON LTD.</p>
        <p>FIRST DELIVERY OF EARLY SPRING MILLINERY AND DRESS FABRICS.</p>
        <p>BRIDGE STREET, WARRINGTON.</p>
