        <head>Examiner, Saturday, March 23, 1907.</head>
        <p>The Examiner, Saturday, March 23, 1907.</p>
        <p>contribution and whilst unemployment undoubtedly exists in our midst it is not present to an extent great enough to justify the committee in opening a public subscription list with the result that little has been done in the direction of alleviating the distress arising through lack of work. The committee recognize that the opening of the Labour Bureau merely expedited the filling of existing vacancies and did not in any way reduce the ranks of the out-of-works, and they are urging the Government to immediately amend the Act, at the same time expressing the opinion that the cost of providing employment should not be depend- ent upon voluntary contributions.</p>
