        <p>BLBCTION ON GUARDIANS. TO THE EIACTORS OF BZW6EY WARD LADIES AND GENIttSMEN, Most people agree that there is need for women on the Board of Guardians. I therefore offer myself to you as a Candidate. My name is, I believe, well-known in the district, and if elected I shall do my best for the poor and Deedy. You may rely upon me to study economy so as not to add unnecessarily to the expenditure of the town. I am, Yours sincerely, AGNES SISIPSON, 104, Bewsey-road, March 11th, 1907.</p>
