        <p>WARRINGTON BLUE COAT CHARITY 80HOOL. 'NOTICE 113 LIERKBY GIVEN, that the TRUSTEES of the ABOVE SCHOOL will, Cr their next Quarterly Meeting, on the 15th day of April next, prooed to elect Four Children (2 Boys and 2 Girls) to Vacancies now existing in the Institution. No Candidate will be eligible unless an application on his or her behalf (forms of which may be obtained from the Clark, at his Office. 3, Winwiclr Street), shall have been made to the Clerk to the Trustees at least fourteen days previous to the day of Iderting. In electing Children, the Trustees make Orphans their first choice. Those deprived of one parent come next in consideration, and after them the children of parents who have the greatest number and the slenderest means. Dated this 22nd day of Match 1937. ;whpiemg HENRY GBH }MALL, Clerk to the Truatepol.</p>
        <p>THE RURAL IDISTKICT COUNCIL OF WARRINGTON. NOTICH IS HIIRRBY GIVAN that the Accounts of the above-named Rural District Council for the half-year ended September 30th, 1916, will, on the 27th day of March, 1907, be deposited at my office, Bewsey Chambers, WArrington ; and such accounts will be opened to be inspected, examined, and copied by any owner of property or ratepayer in the (listed, of the sail Connell at any reasonable hour in the day- time until tbe Bth day of April, 1907. and on the last- mentioned day. at the hour of Ten o'clock in the forenoon, the ACCOUNTS of the Council will be AUDITBD by RRNRST W. HICKS, Req.. District Auditor of the district comprising the above-mentioned Council, at the Boardroom, Workhouse, in Warrington, when and where every such owner of property or ratepayer who may have any objection to any matter contained In the above-mentioned accounts may attend and prefer his objaction, cad the same will be heard and determined by the Auditor. Dated this 20th nay of March, 1007. JAMBS C. SUTTON. Clerk to the Council. Bewsey Chambers, Warrington.</p>
        <p>_ RUNCORN RURAL DISTRICT COUNCIL BLRCTION, 1907. TO THE PAROCHIAL ELKCTORS OF THE PARISH OF STOCKTON HEATH. LADIES AND GENTLEMICN, Several influential Rlectors have approached me with the requef t that I would stand as a candidate to represent this Parish on the Rural District Council; and I haves cos.sented to do so. I have resided within the Rural Area for 16 years, four of which have been spent in the Parish of Stockton Heath. lam folly aware of the needs of this important and gro*ing Pariah and all cluestions electing its welfare, rtqulrements and improvement will always command and receive my close and energetic attention. There are no business claims upon me and my time is entirely at your disposal and it shall be devoted to your interests. Roliclting yoisr votes and support, I beg to remain. Ladies and Gentlemen. Yours obediently, JOHN MYNEKIMB. lull Crest, Stockton Heath, IPh March, 1907.</p>
