        <p>)HESEIIRE COUNTY COUNTY COUNCIL.— EDUCATION DEPARTMENT. ADMISSION OF PUPIL TEACHERS, 1907. AN EXAMINATION will be held about the beginning of May, at various Centres in the County, for Candi- dates who will be not less than 16 years of ago on August Ist, 1907, and who desire to become Pupil Teachers in the County Elementary Education Area, the Non-County Boroughs, or the Urban District of Wallasey. SCHOLARSHIPS FOR INTENDING PUPIL TEACHERS. A number of Scholarships not exceeding twenty, are offered to Boys or Girls who have attained the age of 14 years, and are not over 15 years on or before July 31st, 1907, and without having held a County Scholar- ship have been in attendance at an approved Secondary School for at least two years, if such signify their intention to become Pupil Teachers at the age of 16, or as soon as possible. For further particulars of the above Examinations, and Forms of application to enter for the same (which must be returned on or before the 13th April),apply Rd. P. WARD, Director of Education. County Education Office, City Rd., Chester.</p>
        <p>HVOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN, that the next _lll GENERAL QUARTER SESSIONS of the Peace for the COUNTY OF CHESTER will be held at the COURT HOUSE, KNUTSFORD, in and for the said County, on MONDAY, the Bth day of April next, at Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon, when the Grand Jury will be empannelled. The hearing of all Appeals arising within the Petty Sessional Divisions of Altrincham, Bucklow, Daresbury, Dukinfield, Middlewich, Sandbach, Congleton, North- which, Prestbury, and Stockport,forming the Knutsford District, and the trials of all prisoners committed from such Divisions, will take place at such Sessions. The Grand and Petty Juries for the Knutsford District must be in attendance at the Conrt House, Knutsford, at the opening of the Court on MONDAY, the Bth day of April next, at Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon. THE COURT will be Adjourned to the Castle of CHESTER, on WEDNESDAY, the 10th day of April ' next, at Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon. The hearing 'of all Appeals arising within the Petty Sessional Divisions of Broxton, Chester Castle, Eddisbury, Nant- , wich, Runcorn, Winsford, and Wirral, forming the Chester District, and the trials of all prisoners com- mitted from the last-mentioned Divisions will take place at such Adjourned Sessions. The Grand and petty Juries for the Chester District must be in attend- ance at the Castle of Chester, at the Opening of the Court on WEDNESDAY, the 10th day of April next, at Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon. REGINALD POTTS, Clerk of the Peace for the Comity of Chester. Chester, 18th March, 1907. COUNTY PALATINE OF CHESTER. DISEASES OF ANIMALS ACTS, 1891 to 1903, AND THE DOGS ACT, 1906. CHESHIRE (CONTROL OF DOGS) ORDER, 1907. NTOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN, that the Cheshire 11 County Council, as the Local Authority under the Diseases of Animals Acts, 1894 to 1903, for the County of Chester, excluding the Municipal Boroughs either wholly or partly situate therein, intend at the expiration of 14 days from the date of this notice, to submit to the Board of Agriculture and Fisheries for confirmation the following REGULATIONS, made at al Meeting of the Executive Committee of such Local Authority held at Chester Castle on Thursday, the 14th day of March, 1907, viz. : CONTROL OF DOGS BETWEEN SUNSET AND SUNRISE. I.—Every dog in the district of the Local Authority shall at all times during the period between one hour lafter sunset and one hour before sunrise, be kept by the Owner thereof under control by being : (i.) Confined in a,kennel or other enclosure from which it cannot escape; or (ii.) Secured to some premises by a collar and chain; or (iii.) Accompanied by and under the effectual con- trol of the Owner or other person in charg thereof, such Regulations to apply to the whole of that portion of the County under the jurisdiction of the Committee. AND NOTICE IS HEREBY FURTHER GIVEN, that a copy of such Regulations will be kept at the Office at Chester of the undersigned, the Clerk to such Council, and the same can be inspected by any of the Ratepayers of the County, without fee or reward, any day during office hours for 14 days from the date of the first publication of this Notice. AND NOTICE IS HEREBY ALSO FURTHER GIVEN, that copies of the said Regulations may be obtained at the aforesaid Office, by any Ratepayer of the County, on payment of Sixpence each. Dated this 18th day of March. 1907. REGINALD POTTS, Clerk to the Cheshire County Council. Council Offices, Northgate-street, Chester.</p>
