        <p>A BROKEN-DOWN SYSTEM. This is a condition (or disease) to which doctors give many names, but which few of them really undercand. It is simply weakness—a breakdown, as it were, of tbe vital forces that sustain the system. No matter what may be its causes (for they are aim ast numberless), its symptoms are much the same ; the more prominent being sleeplessness, sense of prostration or weariness, depression of spirits and want of energy for all the ordinary affairs of life. Now, what alone I. absolutely essential in all such cases is INCREASED VITALITY—vigour—VITAL STRENGTH AND ENERGY to throw off these morbid fee:ings, and experience proves that as night succeeds the day this may be more certainly secured by a course of the celebrated life-reviving tonic. THERAPION NO, 3 than by any other known combination. So surely as it is taken In accordance with the printed directions accom- panying it, will the shattered health be restored, the EX- PIRING LAMP OF LIFE LIGHTED UP AFRESH, and a new existence imparted in place of what had so lately seemed worn-out, "used up," and valueless. This wonderful re- storative is purely vegetable and innocuous, Is agreeable to to the taste—suitable for all constitutions and coaditions,in either sex ; and it is difficult to imagine a case of disease or derangement. whose main features are those of debility, that will not be speedily and permanently benefited by this never-failing recuperative essence, which is destined to east, into oblivion everything that had preceded it for ithis wide- spread and numerous class of human ailments. THERAPION may be procured in England at 2s. 9d. and 4. 6. post free, for P. 0., from Mr. R. JOHNSON, 43, HOLFORD SQUARE, LONDON, W.C. Purchasers slued see that the word ' THERAPIOR ' appears on British Government Stamp (In white letters on a red ground) affixed on every package by order of His Majesty's Hon. Comiseioners and Without which It is a forgery.</p>
