        <p>MATRIMONY. ALL those desiring a Matrimonial Alli- ance are requested to communicate, giving personal details and stating precise requirements, with EVELYN LORRAINE, 161 STRAND, LONDON, W.C.</p>
        <p>Association,addressed the meeting and pointed out what valuable work women could do on Boards of Guardians. Women would be able to give the country an immense amount of help in the new Poor Law which she hoped would be passed in the next five years. The law should be firmly administered as regarded the wastrels but more kindly towards the sick, aged and infirm. (Applause.) Mrs. CARRUTHER.S also briefly addressed the meeting. She said she took a keen interest in women and chil- dren, and wanted to do the most she could for them. (Applause). Miss WINSKILL and Nliss BROIDIIENT also spoke.</p>
